{
  "description": "Preview overlay for protocol version 12: the Dijkstra era as the leios-prototype branch of cardano-node runs it (ouroboros-leios tag prototype-2026w36). SELF-CONTAINED: the dijkstra block below is the complete Dijkstra genesis, byte for byte what ouroboros-leios ships, so it stands on its own at any pparamsEpoch. Everything Dijkstra lives here and nowhere else -- the epoch timeline carries no dijkstra block, because no mainnet hard fork has set a Dijkstra parameter yet. In particular the four refScript* parameters are NOT a van Rossem change: cardano-node has shipped them unchanged in configuration/cardano/testnet-template-dijkstra.json since 11.0.1, i.e. before PV11, so they are era defaults and belong with the era, not with a protocol version. (v11-preview.json also carries them, left as-is: it is the historical preview of PV11 and predates this split.) plutusV4CostModel is NOT expressible through this file's `cost_model` block: that block is indexed by the canonical name lists in Profile/Genesis.hs, which cover V1/V2/V3 only, and `genesisCostModels` emits PlutusV1/V2/V3 keys only -- a `cost_model.plutusV4` key here would be dropped in silence by the generic FromJSON for CostModel. It goes in the Dijkstra genesis as a raw 251-entry array instead, which is the mainnet-shape slot for V4 exactly as conway.plutusV3CostModel is for V3. Every value below is copied verbatim from the reference files; none were recomputed. For the record, the V4 array is also derivable: it is the mainnet PlutusV3 251-entry array (data/genesis/mainnet/conway-genesis.json) with the seven van Rossem re-prices from v11-preview's cost_model.plutusV3 applied at plutusV3CostNames positions 54, 64, 65, 66, 119, 135 and 146, which means PlutusV4's first 251 canonical names are PlutusV3's first 251.",
